3 CITY Paarl
3 STAE Cape Colony
3 CTRY South Africa
1 OCCU D. Wessels & Co. Attorney, Notary, and Conveyancer; Member of the Legislative Assembly, Union of South Africa
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 28.07.1873 Matjieskuil was sold by '''Daniel Hendrik Willem Wessels''' to his son-in-law [https://www.geni.com/people/Francois-Dani%C3%ABl-de-Villiers/6000000022697305045 Francois Daniel de Villiers] for £1500 (
2 CONC DO 1873: T456). Philippus Albertus Briers (sr.) purchased Matjieskuil from de Villiers on 18 January 1881 and transported it to his son Philippus Albertus Briers (jr.) on his death in 1913 (DO 1913: T7864).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1885 Joostenberg's Vlakte was owned in undivided shares by Philippus Albertus Briers (sr.) and '''Daniel Hendrik Willem Wessels'''. In that year the said Briers and the said Wessels decided to partition the farm between them, a
2 CONC nd each took transfer of a defined share.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.co.za/books?id=6yszAAAAIAAJ&dq=Wessels+briers+decided+to+partition+the+farm+between+transfer+defined&focus=searchwithinvolume&q=Wessels+decided+partition+between+transfer+defined Source]: Suid-Afrikaanse Hofv
2 CONC erslae, Volume 3. Juta and Company, 1952 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Bought farm Matjieskuil (formerly known as Waarburg), near Klapmuts, dist. Stellenbosch: Purchased from Petrus Johannes Schabort. Together with his brother Jacobus Christoffel Wessels and his aunt's husband, Petrus J. Redelinghuys
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus Christoffel Wessels bought his aunt's husband's (Petrus J. Reedelinghuys †1848) share of Matjieskuil, (formerly known as Waarburg farm), near Klapmuts, dist Stellenbosch in 1847.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Hendrik Willem Wessels purchased his brother's (Jacobus Christoffel Wessels) 2/3 share ownership of Matjieskuil in 1848.
2 CONT
2 CONT He consolidated the farm and sold it to his son-in-law Francois Daniel de Villiers in 1873 who in turn sold it to Philippus Albertus Briers (sr.) on 18.01.1881. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
