1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emigrerar till Nordamerika 1893-05-15
2 CONT
2 CONT * HFL: Bjurholm (AC) AI:10a (1887-1896) Bild 264 / sid 257
2 CONT
2 CONT June 05, 1917. WW1 Registration card at the Town of Lincoln, Marshall Co. Minnesota. Gust Cornelius Holmlund. B: May 29, 1897 in Bjurholm Sweden.  Alien on American soil - Citizen of Canada. Single with no children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 census of Marshall Co. Minnesota states that Gust Holmlund, husband of Julia, was a veteran of WW1.
2 CONT
2 CONT An unidentified child of Gust and Julia has a birth certificate for Oct. 21, 1929.
2 CONT https://www.mnhs.org/people/birthrecords/1929-14601
2 CONT
2 CONT A death certificate exists for HOLMLUND, ANDERS ZAKARIAS, DOD Feb. 16, 1914.  He may be related because he died in Marshall County, MN.
2 CONT https://www.mnhs.org/people/deathrecords/1914-MN-007549
2 CONT He was 75 in the 1905 census.
2 CONT https://www.mnhs.org/people/statecensus/2318138
2 CONT
2 CONT The birthdate of the younger Gust in the 1911 Canadian census around Moosejaw is very close.  No mention of an Anders though.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://automatedgenealogy.com/census11/View.jsp?id=145208&desc=1911+Census+of+Canada+page
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial:
2 CONT Mission Covenant Cemetery 
2 CONT Strandquist
2 CONT Marshall County
2 CONT Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Gust C. Holmlund, 70, of 4837 12th Av. S., a retired lumber worker, died in a hospital Sunday after a short illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held in Strandquist, Minn., his former home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Holmlund had lived here 15 years. He was in charge of the hardwoods department for the Elliott Bay Lumber Co. before he retired about two years ago. In the First World War he served in the Canadian army. In the Second World Wa
2 CONC r he was a Selective Service System worker.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Holmlund was born in Sweden. He came to this country in 1906. He was a member of the Scandinavian Fraternity, the Independent Order of Foresters and the American Legion in Strandquist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife, Jennie; three sons, Ernie, Argyle, Minn., Robert, Chicago, and George L. Holmlund, Racine, Wis.; three daughters, Mrs. Lorraine Setten, Whitewater, Minn., Mrs. Geneva Magaw, San Francisco, and Miss Estell H
2 CONC olmlund, Winona, Minn.; two sisters and two brothers; 14 grandchildren, and two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: ShaneO
2 CONT Record added: Mar 30, 2010 
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 50440240
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/50440240/gust-cornelius-holmlund
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Gustaf Cornelius
2 CONT When Gustaf Cornelius Holmlund was born on 25 May 1887, in Bjurholm, Västerbotten, Sweden, his father, Gustaf Albert Holmlund, was 26 and his mother, Hildur Katarina J. Jonsdotter, was 22. He married Julia Ingelborg Henrietta Lofs
2 CONC trom Holmlund about 1912. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 4 daughters. He immigrated to Minnesota, United States in 1927 and lived in Lincoln Township, Marshall, Minnesota, United States in 1930 and Strandquist, Marsh
2 CONC all, Minnesota, United States in 1940. He died on 23 March 1958, in Seattle, King, Washington, United States, at the age of 70, and was buried in Mission Covenant Cemetery, Strandquist, Marshall, Minnesota.
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/L2VK-T3T/gustaf-cornelius-holmlund-1887-1958
