1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hyman Simons came to South Africa with Cecil Rhodes ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Simons_(academic)])
2 CONT
2 CONT Hyman Simons and Gertrude May Morkel had 5 sons/daughters
2 CONT # Eric Morkel Simons 
2 CONT # Arthur Theodore Simons 
2 CONT # Irene Simons 
2 CONT # Hyman Lionel Simons   
2 CONT # '''Harold Jack Simons'''
2 CONT  who married Ray Alexander Simons
2 CONT
2 CONT Jack Simons (1 February 1907 – 22 July 1995) was a South African university academic and anti-apartheid activist.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ray Alexander Simons née Alexandrowich was born on 12 January 1914 in Latvia. While at school, she displayed little fear in challenging authorities. Her independent thinking suggested she pursue a career in medicine but she soon t
2 CONC ook up politics. When she was about 13, she became active in the underground Latvian Communist Party.
2 CONT
2 CONT She arrived in South Africa on 6 November 1929, and began to organise Black workers unions. Five days later, on 11 November 1929, after meeting Cissie Gool and lifelong friend John Gomas, she joined the Communist Party of South Af
2 CONC rica (CPSA), aged 16.
