1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oliver Osbaldiston BOWKER was born on 27 Sep 1857 'Craigie Burn', Somerset East, Cape of Good Hope. He died on 2 Aug 1951 'Glen Craig', Somerset East, Cape Province, South Africa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Farmer on 'Glen Craig' which was a sub-division of 'Craigie Burn'. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the file of Paul Tanner-Tremaine:
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver lived most of his life on his farm Glen Craig ('Craigie Burn'), Somerset East. He was twice mentioned in despatches during the Anglo-Boer War; first for clearing the Somerset East district of horses so that the Boers could 
2 CONC not get fresh re-mounts and secondly for putting the names of all the farmers and their families on their doors to enable the troops to see 'if they were harbouring Boers.'
2 CONT
2 CONT His grand-daugher Susie-Bell Aylward related the following anecdote. "When the family used to travel to Nylstroom, with her father Stuart driving the old Model T Ford. Oliver used to carry a whistle and if he thought that the road
2 CONC  was not safe, or he could
2 CONT
2 CONT not see around the corners, he would tell Stuart to stop the car, and blow his whistle to warn any oncoming people or traffic!"
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH NOTICE:
2 CONT
2 CONT MOOC 6/9/18651 R5072
2 CONT
