1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Armourer at Jönköping Regiment 1758-08-14. Sergeant at Jönköping Regiment 1760-02-29. Constituted Second Lieutenant 1761-07-29. Confirmation power of attorney (KrAB) 1763-09-21. Transferred to the Kronoberg Regimen
2 CONC t in 1764. First Adjutant of the Kronoberg Regiment 1770-11-20. Lieutenant in the Kronoberg Regiment 1774-03-23. Ennobled 1776-04-24 and adopted into the nobility of his younger brother, Erik Otto (introduced in 1776 under no. 209
2 CONC 0). Second Lieutenant's Division 1776-12-19. Captain in the regiment 1777-06-06. Lieutenant's division 1781-06-01. Parting with the character of the Major (KrAB.) 1784-10-18. Died 1805-06-21 at his estate Målajord in Dädesjö paris
2 CONC h, Kronoberg county childless, and thus closed his own lineage. Adelborg, who was praised by his regimental commander as "a particularly skilful and energetic officer", was present at the war in Pomerania and was for a time comman
2 CONC ded by the Sprengtporten Free Corps. He took part in the battle of Usedom in 1758, in the storming of Wollin in 1759, the affair at Neuensund and the storming of Malchim in 1761.
