1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sanna Cecilia Lundell (born 6 November 1978 in Stockholm, Sweden) is a Swedish freelance journalist and television presenter. She is the daughter of the singer Ulf Lundell.[1] She has done journalistic work for the
2 CONC  magazines Mama, M-Magasin, Hennes, and the Aftonbladet newspaper.[2] She has also been working as a television presenter at TV3 with shows such as Sanning och konsekvens along with Robert Aschberg, and Stalkers with Hasse Aro. Si
2 CONC nce June 2013 she has been presenting the documentary series TV3 Dokumentär.[3][4] She participated as a celebrity contestant in Let's Dance 2019, which was broadcast on TV4[5]
